  "title": "The operator norm of a covector is bounded by a constant times its Euclidean coefficient norm",
  "statement": "For all P, n ∈ ℕ there is a real K > 0 such that ‖α‖ ≤ K·covectorEuclideanNorm α for every α ∈ Covector (Euclid P) n. Here ‖·‖ is the operator norm of continuous alternating maps on ℝ^P, and covectorEuclideanNorm α = (Σ_{I : Fin n → Fin P strictly increasing} α(e_{I(0)}, …, e_{I(n−1)})²)^{1/2} with (e_j) the standard orthonormal basis of ℝ^P.",
